# Salesforce — FieldPilot / GTM Expansion Intelligence

Before any Salesforce or data-model change, read `docs/project-context.md` and treat it as the source of truth for Account, Product, and entitlement models.

## Record type

- FieldPilot Account Record Type API name: `Field_Pilot`
- Current RecordTypeId: `012g7000004KDoPAAW`

## Hierarchy

- **Business Account** = commercial parent / buying entity (`Account.Type = Business`)
- **Location Account** = operational branch (`Account.Type = Location`)
- Connect locations with standard `Account.ParentId` (Location → Business)
- **Opportunities belong to the Business Account**, never to a Location by default
- Location recommendations support evidence; they are not commercially actionable by default

## Product catalog and entitlements

- Product2 is the product catalog
- `External_Product_Code__c` is the cross-system product key
- `Product_Entitlement__c` is the current implemented entitlement model
- Entitlements may exist at Business or Location scope
- Do not assume parent entitlement automatically applies to all locations
- Before recommending products, future logic must account for entitlement coverage
- Do not introduce Asset / Contract / Quote / Order dependencies unless explicitly requested
- Full RLM / Revenue Cloud is deferred for the current MVP
- Do not duplicate the current entitlement model with another custom object without a documented architecture decision
- Detailed schema: `docs/project-context.md` (do not duplicate the full field list here)

## Modeling rules

- Prefer standard Salesforce functionality before introducing new custom fields or objects
- Never introduce a custom field that duplicates a field already documented in `docs/project-context.md`
- Do not store raw product telemetry or raw support history in Salesforce (Snowflake is the system of analysis)
- Do not redesign the Account hierarchy or entitlement model without explicitly updating `docs/project-context.md` in the same change

## Implemented Account field names (authoritative)

| Use these | Do not recreate |
|-----------|-----------------|
| `Account.Type` (Business / Location / Other) | `Account_Scope__c` |
| `NumberofLocations__c` | `Branch_Count__c` |
| `Segment__c` | `Customer_Segment__c` |
| `Service_Verticals__c` (multi-select) | `Service_Vertical__c` |
| `Customer_Id__c` (Business only) | putting Customer Id on Location |
| `Location_Id__c` (Location only) | putting Location Id on Business |
| `Revenue_Weight__c` (Location only) | putting Revenue Weight on Business |
| `Customer_ARR__c` (primarily Business) | inventing authoritative Location ARR |

Full definitions: `docs/project-context.md`.

## Source control and secrets

- Salesforce metadata must remain source-controlled under `salesforce/`
- Never commit Salesforce auth/session information, tokens, or org credentials
